📌 Make sure it doesn't have a nested folder, or updates may not apply properly.

📄 check_response.json
Type: JSON response file

Purpose: Simulates a server API telling the client whether an update is available.

📄 Contains:

json
Copy
Edit
{
  "update_available": true,
  "version": "1.0.1",
  "download_url": "http://192.168.0.100:8000/update.zip",
  "filename": "update.zip",
  "checksum": "abc123..."  // SHA256 of update.zip
}
The rpi_updater.py script fetches this file to determine:

Is an update available?

What version?

Where to download it from?

Is it safe (via checksum)?

📝 Optional Files
📄 version.txt (inside app/ and update.zip)
Purpose: Just a version indicator.

After a successful update, ~/app/version.txt should show the new version (1.0.1).

📄 post_install.sh (optional)
Type: Shell script (inside update.zip)

Purpose: Run any post-install steps (e.g., migration, service setup).

If present in the extracted update, it will be executed after file copy.

📁 Log File (Defined in Config)
Location: /home/pi/rpi_updater.log or /var/log/rpi_updater.log

Purpose: Stores logs of every step like:

Download started/finished

Checksum passed/failed

Backup created

Install success/failure

✅ Summary Table
File/Folder	Role
rpi_updater.py	Main update script (check/download/install/rollback)
update_config.json	Settings like version, paths, update server, logging
app/	Current installed version of your application
backup/	Folder where backups of the app are stored
update_server/	Local HTTP server root folder
update.zip	The zipped package of the new app version
check_response.json	Metadata that declares an update is available
version.txt	Indicates the app version (used for checking updates)
post_install.sh	(Optional) Script to run after update completes


